-- Hand-written migration (NOT generated by `prisma migrate dev` against the
-- live Supabase DB — this project's convention, established in the two
-- prior SDD changes, is that no migration touches the real deployed
-- database without explicit human go-ahead first; this file was prepared
-- by an agent and must be reviewed and run manually).
--
-- Context: the "legacy" discount engine (`engineVersion = 'legacy'` or
-- NULL) never had a real implementation in this code base — only the
-- universal engine (`services/discountEngine/universal`) exists.
-- `services/discountService.js` and `services/salesServices.js` have been
-- changed to no longer execute any rule through a "legacy" path (dead
-- branch removed), and `sanitizeRuleInput` now forces
-- `engineVersion: 'universal'` server-side on every create/update,
-- regardless of what the client sends.
--
-- This migration does two things to match that code change:
--   1. Backfills existing rows so no row is left pointing at the removed
--      path. Confirmed with the product owner: no legacy-tagged
--      DiscountRule is active in production today, so this is expected to
--      affect 0 rows in practice — it is a safety net, not a real data
--      conversion. If a legacy row DOES carry meaningful data in its
--      `conditions` field (not just an empty/inactive row), this blind
--      `engineVersion` flip does NOT translate that data into
--      `conditionsUniversal` — use `node scripts/migrate-discount-rules.js`
--      (dry-run by default) for that instead, BEFORE running this file, if
--      any such row is found.
--   2. Changes the column default from 'legacy' to 'universal' as
--      defense-in-depth for any insert path that does not go through
--      `sanitizeRuleInput` (seeds, manual SQL). The application layer is
--      the real enforcement point; this default is a backstop only.
--
-- Safe to re-run (idempotent): the UPDATE only touches rows that still
-- have the old value, and SET DEFAULT is a no-op if already set.

UPDATE "DiscountRule"
SET "engineVersion" = 'universal'
WHERE "engineVersion" IS NULL OR "engineVersion" = 'legacy';

ALTER TABLE "DiscountRule" ALTER COLUMN "engineVersion" SET DEFAULT 'universal';
